  "kind": "pose",
  "note": "Browsing: the head comes down over foliage in front, works through a run of chews, tugs a mouthful free, settles back and goes on chewing, then lifts. Head pitch is POSITIVE because positive is nose-down. The chew is mostly YAW, not pitch -- a ruminant grinds side to side, and a pure up-down bob reads as a bird pecking. All four feet stay at their rest positions for the whole clip, so the animal is standing still and eating rather than shuffling. The keys at t=0.85 and t=3.65 are identical, as are the two at the ends: the flat pair bracket a loopable munch window the way `sit` and `lie` bracket their hold, so a game can cut this into down / munch / up and hold the middle for as long as the animal is feeding.",
